      "title": "Checksum negative changes mandatory package prefix before checksum guard",
      "evidence": "  const crc=inflateRawSync(good.subarray(10));crc[0]^=1;assert.throws(()=>tarEntries(gzipSync(crc)),/TAR_CHECKSUM/);",
      "static_trace": [
        "tinyTar positive member is package/a.",
        "Header byte0 p(112) XOR1 becomes q(113), producing qackage/a.",
        "TAR_PATH at line253 refuses /^package\\/[A-Za-z0-9_./-]+$/ before TAR_CHECKSUM at line261.",
        "The case expects /TAR_CHECKSUM/, so once setup admits it will not match that earlier refusal. No fixture executed by reviewer."
      ],
      "requested_narrow_fix": "Tamper a checksum octal digit or change only a still-valid basename package/a->package/b without recomputing checksum. Preserve ASCII/path/type/octal/positive and other negatives, caps, guard and case name.",
